<title>USA: CME says SEC rule change lifts regulatory burden.</title>
<headline>CME says SEC rule change lifts regulatory burden.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A letter to Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) members announced that effective next month, mutual funds will be able to deposit margin directly with futures commission merchants (FCMs) to trade futures and options.</p>
<p>The letter, circulated Thursday, said the just-announced Securities and Exchange Commission rule change eliminates an obstacle to the use of futures.</p>
<p>&quot;We have worked aggressively for over a decade to effect this result,&quot; the letter said. &quot;A significant regulatory burden has finally been lifted from the brokerage industry.&quot;</p>
<p>The letter was signed by CME chairman Jack Sandner and president Bill Brodsky.</p>
